{"Working-hours check computes `end` from `slotStartTime` making start/end identical and does not handle the case where there are no working hours for that day (which should be unavailable)": 0.9633480906486511, "Comparison is always false because it compares two different Dayjs object instances with `===`, causing zero-length date overrides (start == end) to never be treated as full-day unavailability, potentially offering incorrect slots": 0.9729837775230408, "When `dateOverrideExist` is true, the function returns `true` immediately, skipping busy checks below, which can mark a slot as available even when it overlaps an existing busy interval": 0.950352668762207, "Date-override check using `dateOverrides.find(...)` returns `false` if it finds any override on the same day where the slot is outside that override, causing slots inside one range to be rejected because they are outside other ranges when a day has multiple override ranges": 0.9164609313011169, "`override.timeZone` is optional in `TimeRange` but is used as a required timezone (`tz(override.timeZone)`), which can throw or compute incorrect offsets if caller passes date overrides without a timezone - should fall back to `organizerTimeZone`": 0.9736082553863525, "Missing regression test for ROUND_ROBIN event with a fixed host + date override that removes availability to verify affected slots are filtered out": 0.3789671063423157}